{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7661","id":5210916375,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABNphGFw","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7661","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7661.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7661.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7661","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7661/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7661/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7661/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/statuses/43a547f69e7dc883f6f29aa064b3033039015351","number":7661,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"research(atlas): boundary-drift measurement for span reuse (#6038)","user":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Closes the measurement deliverable for #6038 (parent #6028); the reuse-safety rule is stated for the span-schema design in #6035.\n\n## What was measured\n\nReal Atlas corpus (114,165 messages scanned, 498,564 candidate targets), deterministic sample of 50 paragraph targets (seed 6038), each embedded in its original window (prev + target + next paragraph) and in 4 perturbed windows, with the production embedder replicated exactly (pinned Snowflake arctic-embed-m-v2.0 ONNX, CLS pooling, prompt-free documents; queries with the production `query: ` prompt) and a fixed set of 20 golden queries. Corpus text stays private — numbers and methodology only.\n\n## Headline numbers\n\n| perturbation | median cosine drift | p95 drift | median \\|Δrank\\| (pool of 50) | top-10 flips |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| boundary shift (1 sentence) | 0.047 | 0.190 | 2 | 6.9% |\n| neighbor replaced (prev) | 0.292 | 0.554 | 7 | 17.8% |\n| neighbor replaced (next) | 0.121 | 0.360 | 4 | 10.3% |\n| target alone (no context) | 0.168 | 0.478 | 5 | 11.9% |\n\n## Reuse-safety rule\n\nA stored span vector may be reused only when the full window text that produced it is byte-identical in the new version; any boundary shift or neighbor change invalidates it and the span must be re-embedded. Full report: `pkgs/atlas-search/eval/boundary-drift-6038.md`; experiment script: `pkgs/atlas-search/eval/boundary_drift_6038.py`.\n\n🤖 queue worker lane code-d, task 13010\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796729240&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7661&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7661&signature=88f53a7e7d4e716a574ef33978064dc9f27077a29da0360f67df00ddd7849864\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-c